2026-01-14 22:07:57,279 - INFO - [20] 来源: Precipitation and transformation of highly dispersed α-Cr phase in Ni3Al-based superalloy (块: None)
Precipitation and transformation of α-Cr phase in Ni3Al-based alloy was studied by using aging heat
treatment. The results showed that clustered and highly dispersed α-Cr phase precipitated at later
aging stage from γ matrix of the alloy which was solution treated with air cooling (SAA) and water
cooling (SWA), respectively. Orientation relationship between α-Cr phase and γ′ was
[−110]α−Cr∥[−110]γ′. Due to the fastest cooling rate of SWA, plenty of vacancies formed which
contributed to the precipitation of highly dispersed α-Cr phase. Supersaturation of Cr element under
SWA was lower than that of SAA, resulting in the delay of α-Cr phase nucleation under SWA compared
with SAA. Chromium-rich γ matrix directly decompose into α-Cr phase, strengthening the Ni3Al-based
alloy by impeding dislocation motion. In addition, no α-Cr phase precipitated from γ matrix during
aging after solution treatment with furnace cooling (SFA) because the precipitation of secondary γ′
between adjacent primary γ′(γI′) during furnace cooling (SF) which consumed Cr elements. Moreover,
γI′ grows directionally with aging time prolonging under SAA and SWA, whereas it remains concave
cube under SFA.

